[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc15
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: PC15’s host routing configuration (default gateway on eth0). Mechanism: Traffic to off-subnet destinations (172.18.50.0/24) must be forwarded to the VLAN 51 gateway. PC15 is configured with default via 172.18.51.250, which does not exist on the segment, so ARP resolution for the next hop fails. The kernel then returns “Destination Host Unreachable,” while same-subnet traffic continues to work because it is directly L2-switched.

Localization and evidence:
- On PC15 eth0: ip route shows “default via 172.18.51.250 dev eth0.” ip neigh shows “172.18.51.250 dev eth0 FAILED,” and ping to 172.18.50.14 returns “From 172.18.51.15 Destination Host Unreachable.” PC15 can ping local hosts (e.g., 172.18.51.17).
- On a healthy peer (PC16): default via 172.18.51.254, and it successfully pings Laptop4 (172.18.50.14). Both PC15 and PC16 cannot reach 172.18.51.250, while PC15 can ping 172.18.51.254 directly, confirming .254 is the valid gateway.

Root cause: PC15’s default gateway is misconfigured to 172.18.51.250 instead of the correct 172.18.51.254.

Corrective fix: Update PC15’s network settings to set the default route to 172.18.51.254 (via DHCP option router or static config) and remove the invalid route (e.g., ip route del default; ip route add default via 172.18.51.254). Optionally flush the failed neighbor entry (ip neigh flush dev eth0). After correction, PC15 should reach 172.18.50.x normally. 
=== END ===